.TH MAKEINFO 1.SH NAMEmakeinfo \- turn Texinfo into Info.SH SYNOPSIS\fBmakeinfo\fR[options] file.texinfo ....SH DESCRIPTIONGNU makeinfo: it reads a Texinfo document and writes the Info file thatGNU Info reads, split into pieces when it is large.  Long options beginwith\fB+\fR.\fR.SH OPTIONS.TP 12\fB+no-split\fRone output file, however large..TP 12\fB+no-validate\fRdo not check node cross-references..TP 12\fB+no-warn\fRerrors only..TP 12\fB+verbose\fRsay what it is doing..TP 12\fB+fill-column\fI n\fRfill to\fIn\fRcolumns, 72 unless told..TP 12\fB+paragraph-indent\fI n\fRindent paragraphs by\fIn\fR,\fR3 unless told..TP 12\fB+footnote-style\fI MN|BN\fRfootnotes as nodes of their own, or at the bottom of the node..TP 12\fB+error-limit\fI n\fR.TP 12\fB+reference-limit\fI n\fRstop after so many errors, or warn about so many references..TP 12\fB+version\fRthe version..SH SEE ALSOtex